  "interpretation_caveat": "K_prod with per-block gammas is mathematically a single anisotropic (two-bandwidth) RBF on the concatenated 8 dims; K_add corresponds to the direct sum of the two block RKHS feature spaces. Both are domain-matched (explicit mobility/network block structure).",
  "verdict": "Domain-matched classical kernels MATCH the quantum cross-layer kernel at matched N: best structured classical (k_product) PR-AUC 0.875 vs qsvm_crosslayer 0.875 (paired grouped-bootstrap delta -0.000, Holm p=1.000); additive 0.869/0.907 and product 0.875/0.924 (PR/ROC) vs quantum 0.875/0.925 and flat 8-dim RBF 0.884. Consistent with the paper's no-advantage line: the cross-layer GAIN over the generic ZZ map reflects structured mobility-x-network interaction that a block-structured CLASSICAL kernel also captures, not a uniquely quantum representation.",
